<p>Heya, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/lonelygray" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6431167); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6431167&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1599441298" alt="LonelyGray" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6431167)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/lonelygray" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6431167); return false;">LonelyGray</a></span>. Welcome to the SCP Wiki!</p>
<p>It's great to see you've been interested in SCPs for so long, and I'm glad to see after all that time, you feel you're ready to start writing yourself. Don't worry if you're not too confident in yourself; there's plenty of on-site resources that will ensure that your writing is up to site standards prior to posting and opening your article(s) up to the voting process. Another great way of knowing what the community is interested in these days is by reading a lot of the newer articles. I personally recommend you check out <a href="/scp-5409">SCP-5409</a> as it's a simple idea with really good execution. Anyway, here are some resources that will help you out in your journey around the site:</p>
